1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,269
The reporter arrived with a photographer, a film crew, a documentary camera, and a question the group could not answer: why does the same failure look different in every home?

2
00:00:12,269 --> 00:00:24,952
A cyclist, a pianist, and a cartoonist gave three different accounts of one afternoon in the clinic, and an ancient habit of counting only the first one won again.

3
00:00:24,952 --> 00:00:29,772
The numbers were a glass wall: transparent and hard.

4
00:00:29,772 --> 00:00:39,961
A user of the service, a client of the council, a debtor on the fifth floor: each had a different estimation of the same wait.

5
00:00:39,961 --> 00:00:43,840
“The constant is care,” Maya said.

6
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:47,340
“Everything else is a bubble.”

7
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:58,114
A spokesman for the council, an interviewer from the radio, and an informant who asked not to be named described the playground as a success.

8
00:00:58,114 --> 00:01:03,558
“A brick, a diamond, and a jewel are all hard,” Lin said.

9
00:01:03,558 --> 00:01:16,897
“Only one of them is the gift of a ruler.” The emperor of that sentence was, he admitted, a fool, and the answer he gave the reporter was a stupid one.

10
00:01:16,897 --> 00:01:25,026
A photographer wrapped a blanket around a child who had been waiting since morning, and took a photo of the queue.

11
00:01:25,026 --> 00:01:30,135
A woman with a bandaged arm waited with a second photo in her hand.

12
00:01:30,135 --> 00:01:37,194
“Certainly you have room for one more,” she said, and the camera turned toward her.

13
00:01:37,194 --> 00:01:42,374
“That is a laugh and a sigh in one gesture,” the assistant said.

14
00:01:42,374 --> 00:01:57,797
“Our transparency is childish,” the designer replied, “and the offender is the system, not the blanket.” A contestant in the queue agreed, and asked for a second blanket.

15
00:01:57,797 --> 00:02:11,310
The recipient of the service, a prisoner on day release, a buyer of the cheapest plan, and an adventurer who had walked the whole route: none of them had been asked for a single line.

16
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:25,183
“A messenger is not a liar,” the spokesperson said, “but a messenger is not a witness either.” The group had its highest increase in trust that week, and its lowest in love.

17
00:02:25,183 --> 00:02:30,928
A patient would have said it better; a friend would have said it more kindly.

18
00:02:30,928 --> 00:02:38,672
The mean version was this: that the subject of the survey had never been the people in it.
